# lib/shaders.warp's rules that run code at compile time, a rule word of extensions/rules/rule_words.warp: the compiler
# keeps them, taken with the module's own (rewrites.warp module_rule_paths; decision library-zero-bake-plan 1b)
// paint(f, width, height) and shader_of(f) quote f with the functions it calls and the values it reads
// (definitions_reached). f may be this program's function or one a `use` names: that module is spliced after these
// rules run, so `is function` is not asked (it is false for the imported name). A name nothing defines as a function
// (a parameter, a shader text) makes definitions_reached return ø, and the paint stays as it is. The WGSL is made at
// run time (lib/shaders.warp)
rewrite paint($f, $w, $h) => paint_function($reached, $w, $h, $f) where $f is symbol and $reached = definitions_reached($f, $program)
rewrite shader_of($f) => shader_of($reached) where $f is symbol and $reached = definitions_reached($f, $program)
